# Resume saved Context

## Section

Import a portable Session before you start the AgentServer. This restores
conversation data, not a pending worker or an execution checkpoint. Change
`backend` to `:live` and set `OPENAI_API_KEY` to continue with a real model.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

mock =
  if backend == :mock do
    {:ok, pid} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: [%{reply: {:text, "The code is ALPHA."}}])
    pid
  end

context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define the Agent

```elixir
defmodule Guide.ResumeContext do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_resume_context"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
      answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default(""),
      messages: Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.schema()
    })

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Use the saved Context."
      reasoning :react
      memory history: :messages

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 1
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.resume_context", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Save and import a Session

```elixir
thread = Jido.Thread.new(metadata: %{system_prompt: "Use the saved case facts."})
saved = Jido.Session.new(id: "saved-case-session", thread: thread)

{:ok, saved} =
  Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.append(saved, [
    ReqLLM.Context.user("Remember the code ALPHA."),
    ReqLLM.Context.assistant("I will remember ALPHA.")
  ])

{:ok, agent} =
  Jido.AI.Agent.from_initial_state(
    Guide.ResumeContext,
    %{messages: saved},
    id: "guide-resumed-agent"
  )

%{saved_session_id: saved.id, imported_session_id: agent.state.messages.id}
```

No model call occurs during import. Start the imported Agent and ask a new
question. The new request uses the saved exchange as Context.

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(agent)
{:ok, answer} = Guide.ResumeContext.ask_sync(server, "What is the code?", context: context)

%{answer: answer, session_id: Jido.AgentServer.agent(server).state.messages.id}
```

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [request]} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
  true = String.contains?(Jason.encode!(request.body), "ALPHA")
end

:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Checkpoint and resume](../v3/20_checkpoint_resume.md). For a paused
ReAct execution, use the separate checkpoint contract instead of initial
Context import.
